    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>54</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#62;</mo></math>&nbsp;be direction ratios of plane containing the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Since plane normal will be perpendicular to given lines then by condition of perpendicular lines,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>On solving&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>35</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>So, DR of plane are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#62;</mo></math></p><p>Now let DR of plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;(as plane normal will be perpendicular to given line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>)</p><p>Now solving equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get, direction ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, equation of plane will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p><p>Now finding distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}